<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Kenmare in second gold venture in Yugoslavia.</title>
<headline>Kenmare in second gold venture in Yugoslavia.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish mineral firm Kenmare Resources Plc said on Monday it signed a second joint venture for gold exploration and development in Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>Kenmare said it would control the board of the joint venture with Geoinstitut, a geological institute with minerals licences.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Projects for exploration included Deli Jovan, on a major gold and copper bearing belt in the Balkans, and Ruplje.</p>
<p>Kenmare said the venture would act in parallel with its previously-announced gold exploration deal with Gemini, its other alliance in Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>--Dublin newsroom 353-1-661-3377</p>
</text>
